                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 396.1–GE/7–2355. Top Secret. Drafted
                    by Bohlen on July 23. For three other accounts of the dinner conversations, see
                        <ref target="#d187">Document 187</ref>, <ref target="#d186"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Supra</hi></ref>, and <ref target="#d188"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">infra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d189-f2" n="2" xml:id="d189-f2-content">
                <p>Bohlen was seated between Khrushchev and Merchant to the right of Secretary
                    Dulles at the table.</p>
            </note>
